{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:horizontal-lift-realizes-horizontal-vector","title":"prop:horizontal-lift-realizes-horizontal-vector","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":669,"body":"","kind":"theorem","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#prop:horizontal-lift-realizes-horizontal-vector","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-space]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-lift-tangent]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:horizontal-lift-of-vector-field]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#lem:vector-field-extension-point]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"prop:horizontal-lift-realizes-horizontal-vector","line":1070,"source":"\\begin{proposition}[Every Horizontal Vector is the Value of a Lift]\n\\label{prop:horizontal-lift-realizes-horizontal-vector}\n\n\\uses{def:horizontal-space, def:horizontal-lift-tangent, prop:horizontal-lift-of-vector-field, lem:vector-field-extension-point, lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec}\n\n\\dcref{ch2:2.25}\n\n\n\nFor $x\\in\\tilde M$ and $v\\in H_x$, there is $X\\in\\mathfrak X(M)$ whose horizontal lift satisfies $\\tilde X_x=v$.\n\\end{proposition}\n\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\sketch Extend $d\\pi_xv$ to a smooth field $X$ on $M$ using Lemma \\ref{lem:vector-field-extension-point}. Its lift satisfies $\\tilde X_x=L_x(d\\pi_xv)=v$ because $v$ is horizontal and $L_x$ is the inverse of $d\\pi_x$ on $H_x$.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proposition</div></section>[Every Horizontal Vector is the Value of a Lift] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-70726f703a686f72697a6f6e74616c2d6c6966742d7265616c697a65732d686f72697a6f6e74616c2d766563746f72\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ahorizontal-space\">↗ def:horizontal-space</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23def%3Ahorizontal-lift-tangent\">↗ def:horizontal-lift-tangent</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23prop%3Ahorizontal-lift-of-vector-field\">↗ prop:horizontal-lift-of-vector-field</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23lem%3Avector-field-extension-point\">↗ lem:vector-field-extension-point</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Ahorizontal-lift-linear-spec\">↗ lem:horizontal-lift-linear-spec</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch2:2.25</span></span><p></p>For <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$x\\in \\tilde M$\">$x\\in \\tilde M$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\in H_x$\">$v\\in H_x$</span>, there is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X\\in \\mathfrak X(M)$\">$X\\in \\mathfrak X(M)$</span> whose horizontal lift satisfies <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde X_x=v$\">$\\tilde X_x=v$</span>.  <p></p><section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch Extend <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d\\pi _xv$\">$d\\pi _xv$</span> to a smooth field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$X$\">$X$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> using Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FappendixA%23lem%3Avector-field-extension-point\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#lem:vector-field-extension-point\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a766563746f722d6669656c642d657874656e73696f6e2d706f696e74\">lem:vector-field-extension-point</a>. Its lift satisfies <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde X_x=L_x(d\\pi _xv)=v$\">$\\tilde X_x=L_x(d\\pi _xv)=v$</span> because <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v$\">$v$</span> is horizontal and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L_x$\">$L_x$</span> is the inverse of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d\\pi _x$\">$d\\pi _x$</span> on <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$H_x$\">$H_x$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:horizontal-lift-of-vector-field","next":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:horizontal-vector-field-not-lift","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-space","title":"def:horizontal-space","label":"def:horizontal-space"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#def:horizontal-lift-tangent","title":"def:horizontal-lift-tangent","label":"def:horizontal-lift-tangent"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#prop:horizontal-lift-of-vector-field","title":"prop:horizontal-lift-of-vector-field","label":"prop:horizontal-lift-of-vector-field"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/appendixA#lem:vector-field-ex